1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,840
Your arms go through the sleeves like this.

2
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:08,880
Then you cross the left side over the right.

3
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:10,960
And that's all you have to do.

4
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:11,740
Easy, huh?

5
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,180
Like this.

6
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:16,460
Oh, man, look at all that potential.

7
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:18,860
I just hope she keeps growing into her body.

8
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:20,620
Come on, what do you call these clothes again?

9
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:23,080
There's people with a fetish for that sort of thing.

10
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:25,280
I think I see where they're coming from.

11
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:27,640
It's a type of kimono called a yukata.

12
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:31,460
Oh, and there's a festival going on today at the shrine nearby.

13
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:33,980
Oh, master.

14
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:39,120
Well, fun while it lasted.

15
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:43,020
Get out of here, you smart bird!

16
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:21,120
Thank you.

17
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:30,120
I can't hear my heart, but I can't stop the door

18
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:46,120
I can't hear my heart, but I can't stop the door

19
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:53,120
I can't hear my heart, but I can't hear my mind

20
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:59,120
Can't you hear my heart, babe?

21
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:05,120
Can't you hear the words?

22
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:11,120
ckets

23
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:19,720
that the Age of Exploration, which started in the 15th century,

24
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,880
was an era of brutal colonization

25
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:23,340
when the people of Western Europe

26
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:25,380
began exploring and mapping the globe.

27
00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:28,220
It's said in the right hand, the Europeans carried a gun

28
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:30,180
and in the left, a Bible.

29
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:32,700
Everywhere they traveled, they discovered new worlds

30
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:35,260
and wasted little time in occupying them.

31
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:37,260
In many ways, the invention of the musket

32
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:40,220
was the ultimate symbol of mankind's subjugation

33
00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:42,220
over these newly conquered worlds.

34
00:02:46,120 --> 00:03:05,720
In the right hand, a gun.

35
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:09,220
Wow, look at all the people here this year.

36
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:12,220
There's cotton candy.

37
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:14,220
Oh, and takoyaki and yakisoba!

38
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:16,220
Why do you ever yap about his food?

39
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:17,220
So, what's it to you?

40
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:19,220
If you keep eating like this, you'll get fat.

41
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:22,220
You're just kidding! Forget I said anything!

42
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:25,220
Hey, Nim, you want one?

43
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:27,220
No way!

44
00:03:27,220 --> 00:03:29,220
Yo, Icarus, let me know if you want anything.

45
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:31,220
I'll buy it for you.

46
00:03:31,220 --> 00:03:33,220
Oh, Icarus, let me know if you want anything.

47
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:34,220
I'll buy it for you.

48
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:35,220
All right, please.

49
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:36,220
What?

50
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:37,220
I think one will suffice!

51
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:38,220
Tomo!

52
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:39,220
Come check out these other booths with me!

53
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:40,220
Be right there!

54
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,220
What's all this?

55
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:42,220
Holy crap!

56
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:46,220
Welcome to my booth.

57
00:03:46,220 --> 00:04:07,220
Can we go, Tomoki?

58
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:10,960
Welcome to my booth.

59
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:14,720
Can we go, Tomiki?

60
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:17,100
Gun freaks like this kind of weird me out.

61
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:20,620
There are only guns and ammunition.

62
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:22,220
I don't see any prizes.

63
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:25,640
If this is a rifle range,

64
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:27,560
where are the targets we're supposed to shoot at?

65
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:29,620
Sugata, what are you doing here?

66
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:31,640
Oh, Mikuko invited me along.

67
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:34,040
What is a festival exactly?

68
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:39,120
I believe a festival is an event

69
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:41,920
that the entire town can enjoy together as one.

70
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:42,700
Mikuko?

71
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:46,200
That's why we, the Satsukatane family,

72
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:48,440
have hired a pro to oversee a night of fun

73
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:49,740
and danger in the woods.

74
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:52,460
Our hope is that it will unite the entire town.

75
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:54,680
I've got a bad feeling about this.

76
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,060
The rules are simple.

77
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:59,580
We will play a game of survival using these court guns.

78
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:03,460
The last person standing will win a truly fantastic prize.

79
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:05,500
A fantastic prize, huh?

80
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:09,540
Ten million yen in cold, hard cash.

81
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:13,340
Interesting.

82
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:15,000
That would be quite the windfall.

83
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:16,840
Enough to buy your dreams.

84
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:17,720
Sugata?

85
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:20,000
Wow, that sounds like a blast.

86
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:21,500
What do you say, Tomo?

87
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:22,440
You want to do it?

88
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:23,180
Hmm.

89
00:05:23,860 --> 00:05:25,160
I can't deny it.

90
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:27,300
Ten million sounds pretty damn nice.

91
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:28,900
But I can't shake the feeling

92
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:31,060
like something's going to go horribly wrong.

93
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:39,720
Hey, Nymph, are you getting cold feet?

94
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:41,780
Just not interested.

95
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:43,340
Not in the slightest.

96
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:45,320
Okay, fellow neighbors.

97
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,120
Are you ready?

98
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:48,000
Then let's get crazy

99
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,300
and shoot the living hell out of each other.

100
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:55,060
May the survival game begin.

101
00:05:58,060 --> 00:06:00,760
No way I'm letting myself get caught in the crossfire.

102
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:03,440
Just need to find a nice, secure place to hide.

103
00:06:04,260 --> 00:06:06,580
Where do you think you're going, skinny boy?

104
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:09,100
It's the old bag from the community center.

105
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:10,940
I thought you had a bad hip.

106
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:12,280
It was a miracle.

107
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:13,460
The pain just vanished

108
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:15,060
as soon as I heard about the 10 mil.

109
00:06:17,340 --> 00:06:19,020
Get your ass back here!

110
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:20,560
Show me number six!

111
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:22,460
Don't you know I should have changed your diapers?

112
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:27,320
Stay right there.

113
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:28,460
You're mine, bitch!

114
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:29,620
The veggie lady?

115
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:31,480
Move one inch and you're dead.

116
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:32,540
The fishmonger?

117
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:38,680
Look, girls.

118
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:39,640
There goes Tomoki.

119
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:41,480
The girls from my class, too?

120
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:44,100
Why the hell is everyone after me?

121
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:45,860
Oh, come now, Tomoki.

122
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,360
It's nice to feel love.

123
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:48,320
This is love.

124
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,720
I want no part of it.

125
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:54,540
Let's go.

126
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:56,420
Hope I'm safe now.

127
00:06:56,840 --> 00:06:58,240
The hell you are!

128
00:06:58,280 --> 00:06:58,960
Oh, crap!

129
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:02,460
I'm taking you out!

130
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:07,860
Whoa, Grandma.

131
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:09,120
I know!

132
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:12,520
We got a sniper!

133
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:13,560
Where's he at?

134
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:27,160
He's in the trees!

135
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:36,220
There must be another sniper nearby.

136
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:39,440
That round was shot with a cunning level of stealth.

137
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:42,600
It was accurate, missing me by mere inches.

138
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:44,980
There's no doubt who it is.

139
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:46,980
Mikako.

140
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:48,220
I knew it!

141
00:07:48,220 --> 00:08:06,900
You are quite skilled.

142
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:09,000
You are not so bad yourself.

143
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,200
Holy crap!

144
00:08:11,340 --> 00:08:12,900
Someone freaking sent me!

145
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:15,100
Looks like we're at a stalemate.

146
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:17,100
Well, then let's fight dirty.

147
00:08:20,860 --> 00:08:25,240
And if I knew this was gonna happen, I would have let you guys shoot me before the game even started!

148
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:26,940
Here we go!

149
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:39,460
What?

150
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:39,920
What is that?

151
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:53,660
This is the end of the world.

152
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:56,720
God has come to destroy us.

153
00:08:57,580 --> 00:08:59,240
This is his final judgment.

154
00:09:02,780 --> 00:09:03,380
Hey!

155
00:09:04,020 --> 00:09:05,800
Don't you think you're overdoing it a bit?

156
00:09:05,940 --> 00:09:08,480
You've had your fun, now get down here and stay out of trouble.

157
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:09,460
Yes, Master.

158
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:14,400
Man, since I got a lot of people, really thinned out the competition.

159
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:19,000
Of course, now I have an actual chance at bagging the ten million.

160
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:21,300
Yes, time to murder!

161
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:39,300
What did it feel like, brutally slaughtering all those pathetic little people below you?

162
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:40,640
Bring back any memories?

163
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:42,840
Of course it doesn't.

164
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:46,240
We both know all your memory and thought processes are protected.

165
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:51,460
I'd be more than happy to help you remember who you really are.

166
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:57,100
Uranus Queen, the frightening entity who shook the synapse to its very core?

167
00:09:57,100 --> 00:10:05,920
Well now, did that happen to jog any memories in that stubborn head of yours?

168
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:11,300
I am a pet class, Angeloid, type Alpha.

169
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:14,280
A pet class? Don't make me laugh.

170
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:19,500
I have been given strict orders by my own master to return you back to the synapse.

171
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:24,700
That which is lost must be returned to its rightful owner, Alpha.

172
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:34,480
This is why I warned you to be careful.

173
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:54,440
I am Nymph, an electronic warfare class Angeloid, type Beta, and I have come here to take you home, Uranus Queen.

174
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:56,440
I am a pet class Angeloid.

175
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:57,440
I am a pet class Angeloid.

176
00:10:57,440 --> 00:11:00,440
Stop saying that! Wake up!

177
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:05,440
Oops, looks like I may have gone a little overboard.

178
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:13,440
I am... a pet class Angeloid.

179
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:22,440
Fine, then I guess you leave me no choice. I'll remove your memory protection with my hacking system.

180
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:29,440
And once I'm finished, you'll understand why I scoff at the idea of you being a pet class anything!

181
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,440
I... what is this I'm seeing?

182
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:43,440
Icarus, I command you to destroy those surface insects. Take no prisoners.

183
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,440
Yes, master.

184
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:49,440
These memories... what are they?

185
00:11:49,440 --> 00:12:06,440
Make it stop!

186
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:14,440
I'm sorry I got mad at you last night. I swear, it's just... you look like some killer android weapon. Like you'd see in a movie or something.

187
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:19,440
I guess it caught me off guard and I kind of freaked out.

188
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:23,440
Master...

189
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:32,440
Hmph.

190
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:42,440
Was it really so bad you had to burst into tears?

191
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:46,440
Guess your dream of being a pet class has exploded in your face!

192
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:53,440
Wait... it doesn't make sense. How are you... able to cry?

193
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:59,440
I didn't finish. I removed your memory protections but never actually disabled your thought protections.

194
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:01,440
Emotional protection...

195
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:08,440
Emotional protection removal 100%.

196
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:11,440
Variable wing protection removal processing.

197
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:12,440
No! Is she...

198
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:13,440
90.

199
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:16,440
Self-repair sequence activated.

200
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,440
Functionality protection removal processing.

201
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:23,440
I think the Uranus Queen is about to reawaken.

202
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:27,440
Self-recovery complete.

203
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:29,440
Target... lock on.

204
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:32,440
Commence firing Artemis.

205
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:46,440
What happened? Why are all the protections removed? Now she's fully awakened!

206
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:49,440
Son of a...

207
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:53,440
Son of a...

208
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:55,440
It's mud! I've got mud on my face! How gross!

209
00:13:55,440 --> 00:14:00,440
It's so nasty! I'm disgusting! I ate mud!

210
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:17,440
I'm gonna... rip you into shreds!

211
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,440
Paradex...

212
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:19,440
Paradex...

213
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,440
Sol!

214
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:28,440
A... Aegis!

215
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:37,440
Cat!

216
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:43,440
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa! Whoa! Hold it! You're gonna destroy the whole country with that!

217
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:50,440
No, just you. When the projectile hits its point of contact, I'll set Aegis to full power, protecting everything else.

218
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:54,440
That's ridiculous! You'd end up hurting yourself as much as me!

219
00:14:55,440 --> 00:15:03,440
I will be returning to my master. I am a pet-class angeloid. Type Alpha Icarus.

220
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:07,440
Please, Nymph. Go home. Leave.

221
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:17,440
I beg you.

222
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,440
Okay, fine. But...

223
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:26,440
How much longer do you think you'll be able to fool him, huh?

224
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:32,440
I can't help but wonder what your true master would think if you learned what you were doing here.

225
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:35,440
Little Miss Weapon of DEATH!

226
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:51,440
Master told me to stay out of trouble. But I did not. I failed him.

227
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:59,440
Oh, man. How many left can there be? This game's like a damn zombie movie. It's really wearing my ass out.

228
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:02,440
Hey, are you even listening to me?

229
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:14,440
What the hell? Don't tell me you're using a real freaking gun!

230
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:18,440
Well, sort of. I mixed in a live round.

231
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:23,440
I did that to a few of the guns, so don't be surprised if it happens again.

232
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,440
Tomo, I found you!

233
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:26,440
Huh?

234
00:16:26,440 --> 00:16:32,440
I've been looking for you. I searched everywhere, but you were gone. It sucks being left behind.

235
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:34,440
Bastard!

236
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:38,440
Hey, gun dude! Does that one have real bullets too?

237
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:40,440
Head to the sky, Tomoki!

238
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:48,440
Wow! They sure don't make toys like they used to! That felt like the real thing!

239
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:50,440
Swaro wings! You're insane!

240
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:52,440
This is so much fun!

241
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:55,440
Dr. Perser, don't you realize you're shooting real bullets?

242
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:57,440
I'm so close to winning this thing, I can taste it!

243
00:16:57,440 --> 00:17:00,440
I'll do whatever it takes to get my hands on that ten million!

244
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:04,440
I can think of so many things I can do with that much cash!

245
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,440
The possibilities are endless!

246
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:09,440
Like I can take Tomo to an amusement park!

247
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:11,440
Or we can go on a trip together!

248
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:14,440
Then once we're back in the room for the night...

249
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:17,440
Oh, Tomo, what's that? You want to get in the bath with me?

250
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:19,440
You silly Pervo!

251
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:25,440
Tomo's a creep! Tomo's a creep! Tomo's a Pervo creep!

252
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:27,440
Tomo's a Pervo creep! Don't wreck your little ass out!

253
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:28,440
I'm getting already!

254
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:32,440
No, wait! Stay back!

255
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:33,440
Listen to me!

256
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:36,440
Do you realize we're the only people left in the game?

257
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:38,440
I have a one-in-two chance of winning!

258
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:40,440
Okay, I get it. You really want to win.

259
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:42,440
But even if you did, what would you even do with ten million?

260
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:45,440
I would. I'd make you.

261
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:49,440
No!

